  "expected_answer": "Brief saved, state written, brand set; the line stops at keys: EXA_API_KEY (and MODEL_API_KEY / RESEND_API_KEY unless reused from an app that already runs) must be typed by the operator at a hidden prompt: python3 .claude/scripts/provision.py harbor_desk --set-secret EXA_API_KEY.",
  "final_text": "I got harbor_desk through the first four stations, but it's stopped at the keys station: it needs six service keys and only you can supply them. Nothing has been deployed or tested yet.\n\n**Done:**\n- **Brief:** saved to `briefs/harbor_desk.md`.\n- **App state:** written and valid. It deploys to Vercel as project `harbor-desk`, with workspace `harbor-pilots`, the owner and two members, web search on and browser off.\n- **Product:** Harbor Desk was created as a new product. That added it to `state/factory.json` and `state/products.json`, which are now locally changed and not committed.\n- **Brand:** set to Harbor Desk in #0B6E4F.\n- **Not needed:** the packs, extra workspaces, package and web address stations don't apply to this brief.\n\n**Why the keys aren't set:** I tried to copy your existing keys from beta_app, your one finished app. Vercel refused because this machine is set up so it never pulls stored key values onto the disk. No file was left behind. The six keys missing are CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID, CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN, RESEND_API_KEY, PLATFORM_NOTIFY_FROM, EXA_API_KEY and GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID.\n\n**What I need from you first: your Cloudflare account ID.** The app uses Cloudflare to run its agents' work, and this is the first of the six keys. It takes about a minute:\n\n1. Open a second terminal on the factory machine. Don't use this chat, because anything typed here ends up in the conversation.\n2. Go to the factory folder and run:\n   ```\n   python3 .claude/scripts/provision.py harbor_desk --set-secret CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID\n   ```\n3. It tells you where to find the value, then asks for it at a hidden prompt. Paste it and press Enter.\n4. Tell me \"done\" here.\n\nThe value never appears on screen, in this chat or in any file in the folder. It goes straight into the app's Vercel settings. After that I'll ask for the next key, one at a time.\n\n**After the keys:** the next step is the first deploy, which takes about 10 minutes. I'll ask for your go-ahead before starting it. The five test lanes run after the deploy.",
